@startuml donor-layout
' Revision 2026-10-12: R-OPERATOR custody and explicit retention; R-WORKPLACE service controls, helper-v1 activation and execution-level stops; Draft, no renderer/qualification evidence.
title Donor state layout - Draft target; A/C donor-owned state root; B platform root / separate provisioner pending and disabled
left to right direction
node "Donor machine\nA/C: donor UID; B: root-provisioned separate UIDs" as D {
  folder "Variant root (D0)\nA/C donor-owned; B system-owned" as Root {
    artifact "libexec / lib / releases/<release>\npinned executable/runtime bytes\nA/C donor-owned; B root-owned read-only" as Binaries
    artifact "etc / locked configuration\nbinding, tuple, policy generation, sandbox revision\nA/C donor-owned; C harness write denied\nB bridge-role configuration files" as Config
    folder "services/swarma-bridge-<project>\nA/C donor UID; B bridge UID home" as BridgeHome {
      artifact "Three role-separated keys\nA/C Secure Enclave signing/SSH on qualified Macs\n0600 files elsewhere; K_enc X25519\nB 0600 Ed25519 signing/SSH; no Keychain" as Keys
      artifact "Bridge-owned audit, budgets, lifecycle marks\ndurable cursors/dedup and queued results\ncredential source metadata/store (CIP-0010)" as State
      artifact "Pinned root/operator chain, host CA trust\n@cert-authority; short user certificate\nvariant, tuple, generation, binding" as Trust
    }
    folder "workers/worker-<project>\nA/C donor UID; B harness UID home" as WorkerHome {
      artifact "Managed home + scratch\nprovider native state by admitted credential source\nharness logs retained where required" as Home
    }
    folder "run\nlocal authenticated relay socket\nB peer UID checked; C sandbox allows socket" as Socket
  }
  component "Bridge service / supervisor\nA/C user service; B system daemon\nowns SSH client, signer, admission" as Bridge
  component "Harness + stdio relay\nB harness UID; A/C donor UID\nrelay no keys/network" as Harness
  component "Provider proxy\nB bridge UID or system service; C qualified proxy\nA absent" as Proxy
  component "B privileged provisioner / kernel boundary\naccounts, egress, sandbox, service journal\nseparate spec/name/schema pending" as Provisioner
}
node "Project host" as P {
  artifact "Root-controlled sshd policy\nTrustedUserCAKeys + user-certificate KRL\nprotected relay-only forced command + fixed no-startup-file login shell\nno PTY/forward/rc/env" as SSHPolicy
  artifact "Project registry / keeper-owned trust\nadmission, public worker keys, grants/revocations\nhost CA authority; user CA private key in keeper/hardware token" as Registry
  artifact "Service-principal project bridge / swarma-rb-exec state\noutside workplace UID write/signal authority\nmailbox/cursors; durable identity/digest claims + admission floors\nseparate ten-minute output cache; closed-schema service metadata\ncarrier credential stays project-side" as Mailbox
}
Bridge --> Keys : sign / decrypt / SSH; private keys never sent
Bridge --> State : persist before acknowledgments / termination
Bridge --> Trust : validate CA/name/validity/KRL on each connect
Bridge --> Config : validate current generation / binding before exec/resume
Bridge --> Binaries : absolute paths; verify digest; changed/unreadable/shadowed -> refuse
Bridge --> Harness : consume caller-composed qualified plan
Harness --> Home : B/C managed home + scratch writable
Harness --> Socket : only admitted local relay
Socket --> Bridge
Harness --> Proxy : B/C provider path only
Bridge --> SSHPolicy : one donor-originated SSH; expired/revoked/wrong principal -> refuse
SSHPolicy --> Mailbox : relay to service socket; kernel peer UID + active generation
Registry --> SSHPolicy : user certificates/KRL; retirement stops renewal and closes sessions
Provisioner --> Root : B journaled provision/remove only allocated artifacts; failure -> reverse rollback
note bottom of BridgeHome
  State/keys unreadable to B harness UID and C sandbox.
  A shares UID: no OS confidentiality/integrity/egress guarantee.
  Project claims persist before mutation; floors advance before claims may be discarded.
  Recovery reconciles claim/floor evidence before admission; unknown keeps binding closed.
  Workplace jobs use dispatcher/root launcher/start receipt/exec.stop; v1 applied network before activation.
  Write scope = UID writable set; loopback qualification mandatory; controls never workplace-owned.
  Project retirement deletes home after process absence and declared-key cleanup;
  export only closed-schema service metadata with no agent-controlled content.
  Separate explicit home retention states confidentiality is not guaranteed.
  Exact key/state/audit/cursor file names, socket basename, schema and retention
  unspecified in spec CIP-0009 D0/D1/D5; folders above are the named D0 layout.
end note
note bottom of P
  R-OPERATOR project operator: swarma-operator, no harness; protected broker v0 software root.
  Operator device key stays in phone secure element; phone-signed exact acts over
  pinned-key SSH/tailnet, forced operator command/no shell. Terminal password sudo fallback,
  timestamp_timeout=0, no NOPASSWD. Widening authenticates + confirms, refuses agent sessions;
  includes explicit home retention. Narrowing authenticates only; phone revoke one biometric.
  Reads via mandatory swarma-observer without confirmation; no mutation authority.
  Phone-key lifecycle/operator formats unpublished; user CA custody remains as shown.
  [[../CIP-0011-credential-broker-and-agent-users.md#5-curator-broker R-OPERATOR custody and act rules]]
end note
note bottom of WorkerHome
  Stop keeps bridge/keys; leave keeps keys/config; purge removes only owned artifacts,
  retains donor-visible audit, preserves A/C donor account. Offline revoke outcome unknown.
  [[../CIP-0009-donor-side-deployment-and-bridge.md#recommendation CIP-0009 D0-D3/D5/D7/D12]]
  [[../../protocol/remote-worker.md#trust-and-ssh CA trust]]
  [[../../protocol/remote-worker.md#tools-mailbox-and-lifecycle Lifecycle/ownership]]
end note
@enduml
